<article class="env-lemma" id="0CKM">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0CKM">Lemma <span data-tag="0CKM">9.13.3</span>.</a> Let $K/F$ and $L/F$ be field extensions. Let $\sigma _1, \ldots , \sigma _ n : K \to L$ be pairwise distinct morphisms of $F$-extensions. Then $\sigma _1, \ldots , \sigma _ n$ are $L$-linearly independent: if $\lambda _1, \ldots , \lambda _ n \in L$ not all zero, then $\sum \lambda _ i\sigma _ i(\alpha ) \not= 0$ for some $\alpha \in K$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Apply Lemma <a href="/tag/0CKL" data-tag="0CKL">9.13.1</a> to the restrictions of $\sigma _ i$ to the groups of units. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>